// expect: A=332
// Regression: byte parameters were silently always zero.
//
// Arguments are pushed as full 16-bit words, and words on this machine are
// big-endian. Loading a byte parameter with MOVB at the slot address therefore
// fetched the HIGH byte, which is always 0 for a value below 256. Narrowing now
// happens at the call site, while the value is still in a register.
//
// 77 + 255 = 332
word take(byte a, byte b) {
    return a + b;
}

word main() {
    return take('M', 255);
}
